  "description": "identity.created v2 signing bytes (avalon_protocol::identity_id::identity_created_signing_bytes_v2): UTF-8 of 'avalon:identity.created:v2:{identity_id}:{public_key_hex}:{display_name}'. The display name is last, so a ':' in it is harmless; it is taken as-is (multi-byte UTF-8 stays UTF-8, no normalisation). The public key is lowercase HEX in the signing bytes and standard BASE64 on the wire. The signature is Ed25519 by the identity's inception key over the bytes (verified strictly).",
